<title>UK: Tarmac has 10.5 mln stg profit post-charge.</title>
<headline>Tarmac has 10.5 mln stg profit post-charge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)pre-except  *5.5		   vs 7.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.5		    vs 2.5</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 5.5		    vs 5.5</p>
<p> Pretax pre-except	75.5		   vs 67.1</p>
<p> Pretax		     10.5		   vs 20.3</p>
<p> Turnover		   2.66 bln	     vs 2.48 bln</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the British heavy building materials and construction service group is Tarmac Plc. Analysts had forecast pretax profit before exceptional items of between 46.5 million stg and 68 million stg. The post-exceptional profit accounts for a 65 million stg restructuring charge.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
